Description: Put applications into their systemd scope before they start.
 GNOME Shell, gnome-session and gnome-settings-daemon ask systemd to move each application they launch with
 GDesktopAppInfo into a scope of its own, app-gnome-<application ID>-<pid>.scope, but only once GLib has started it.
 systemd moves only the process it is given, so every process the application started in the meantime stays in the
 cgroup of the service which launched it. Chromium and Electron applications start their zygotes and their GPU
 process at once, which then stay in GNOME Shell's or gnome-session's cgroup, are stopped with it before the
 application at logout, and the application crashes when they go.
 .
 GLib asks systemd for the scope itself instead, right after it spawned gio-launch-desktop, and gio-launch-desktop
 waits until systemd has moved it into the scope before it executes the application, which therefore starts every
 process of its own in the scope. The launching process sends the request before the launch call returns, and
 gio-launch-desktop does not depend on it afterwards, so this holds also when the launching process exits right
 after launching or never runs its main loop again. Over a pipe, the launching process tells gio-launch-desktop
 when systemd refused to create the scope, so that it does not wait in vain. gio-launch-desktop waits 5 seconds at
 most, so that an application starts even when the scope is never created and the launching process could not tell.
 .
 The scope is requested only by processes managed by the systemd user instance, and outside of sandboxes. It has
 the name gnome-desktop's gnome_start_systemd_scope() gives it, so that a launching process which still asks for it
 afterwards fails without moving any process, and gnome-session's drop-in for app-gnome-*.scope applies. The
 "launched" signal names the scope as "systemd-unit" in its platform data, so that launching processes can leave
 the scope to GLib.
Author: Mitar
Bug: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/glib/-/merge_requests/1596
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-06

